    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That seems a bit pretty strict. If an employee wants to use our internal Slack channels or company forums to advocate for social justice causes or human rights issues—things that are part of their identity—would that also be banned under this \"strict neutrality\" rule? Wouldn't that actually make the workplace feel less inclusive for those groups?",
