      "content": "I hear you on the \"echo chamber\" risk, but it feels like this policy assumes that \"political mobilization\" is inherently bad or disruptive. If we ban all expression related to human rights or social justice, aren't we essentially saying that the only way to be \"inclusive\" is to ignore the systemic issues that many of our employees actually care about? Is there really a neutral middle ground here, or is this policy just a way to prioritize the status quo over actual progress?",
